aul sent his salutation (Rom. 16:5). He is spoken of as “the first fruits of Achaia” (R.V., “of Asia”, i.e., of proconsular Asia, which is probably the correct reading).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"mary_1942","name":"Mary","also":"","summary":"A Christian at Rome who treated Paul with special kindness (Rom. 16:6).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6]},{"id":"andronicus_265","name":"Andronicus","also":"","summary":"Man-conquering, a Jewish Christian, the kinsman and fellowprisoner of Paul (Rom. 16:7); “of note among the apostles.”","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"junia_1764","name":"Junia","also":"","summary":"(Rom. 16:7), a Christian at Rome to whom Paul sends salutations along with Andronicus.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"amplias_241","name":"Amplias","also":"","summary":"A Roman Christian saluted by Paul (Rom. 16:8).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[8]},{"id":"stachys_2774","name":"Stachys","also":"","summary":"Spike; an ear of corn, a convert at Rome whom Paul salutes (Rom. 16:9).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"urbane_2894","name":"Urbane","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"apelles_273","name":"Apelles","also":"","summary":"A Christian at Rome whom Paul salutes (Rom. 16:10), and styles “approved in Christ.”","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[10]},{"id":"aristobulus_307","name":"Aristobulus","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[10]},{"id":"herodion_1508","name":"Herodion","also":"","summary":"A Christian at Rome whom Paul salutes and calls his “kinsman” (Rom. 16:11).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"narcissus_2151","name":"Narcissus","also":"","summary":"Daffodil, a Roman whom Paul salutes (Rom. 16:11). He is supposed to have been the private secretary of the emperor Claudius.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"persis_2317","name":"Persis","also":"","summar